+# Publish queue item atomic outputs audit — rev0843
+
+This audit records the rev0843 hardening of `scripts/publish_queue_item.py`. The public release snapshot, JSON record, and Markdown companion now use same-directory atomic writes, and a normal queue-transition failure removes the newly created publication outputs.
+
+- Status: `publish_queue_item_atomic_outputs_validated`
+- Script SHA-256: `358f98921ef01e42c154ae9a2a590d16901bb507a3259b0f8246a419e0937c8b`
+- Validator: `scripts/validate_publish_queue_item_atomic_outputs_rev0843.py`
+- Validator return code: `0`
+
+## Runtime behavior added
+
+- Release outputs are written through a temporary file in the target directory.
+- File data is flushed and fsynced before `os.replace`.
+- The release snapshot path is checked for pre-existence before writing.
+- If `transition_queue_item.py` fails after writes, newly created snapshot/record/note outputs are removed and the command fails with a rollback message.
+
+## Validator output
+
+```text
+publish-queue-item-atomic-outputs-rev0843: OK
+```
+
+## Limit
+
+This is not a full multi-file transaction under process kill or storage failure. It materially improves the ordinary failure path without weakening the rights gate.
